> for example, you find a ring of invisibility and put it on.  

That will make you invisible.

> while invisible, quaff a potion of invisibility, 

That won't make you any more invisible than you already are, but if you
take off the ring now you'll still be invisible until the potion wears
off. (Note: a blessed potion of invisibility doesn't ever wear off)

> read a scroll, 

There's no scroll of invisibility. There's an invisibility spell,
though. If you cast that you're temporarily invisible, like quaffing a
non-blessed potion.

> zap a wand of the same, etc.  

Zapping a wand of invisibility *at yourself* makes you permanently
invisible, like quaffing a blessed potion.

> I thought there was a small chance you would get
> that gain that intrinsic.

No; the chance is 100% and whether or not it's permanent is completely
predictable.

Put on a ring or a cloak of invisibility - invisible until you take it
off
Drink a cursed or uncursed potion of invisibility or cast an
invisibility spell - invisible until it wears off (a cursed potion
makes monsters notice you the moment you drink it; "For some reason,
you feel your presence is known")
Drink a blessed potion of invisibility or zap yourself with a wand of
invisibility - permanently invisible.
 
